title: Authorizations › Worklist › What makes a row
route: /authorizations
intro: The worklist stores nothing. Its rows are worked out from what the demo already holds, one row per request: the open queue requests, the approved-authorization ledger, the Dashboard requests, the saved New Case drafts and the accepted denials. A queue request and its ledger record are the same request, so they share one row. The rows are then kept to the sites in view and put in order.
dir: TD
also: Demo only, Both sites at the start: 56 open queue requests (24 of them also have a ledger record), 32 approved authorizations with no open request, and 7 open denials that are in neither list: 95 rows. The 5 saved drafts all belong to queue requests, so they add no row. A row keeps its sources, so the quick views, the case page and the review drawer open the same records as before.
---
start s0 "The list is drawn, or anything it reads changes\n(a send, a payer reply, a signature, a draft saved, the demo clock)"

group gS "Sources, in this order"
  process r1 "**1 Open queue requests**\nPreparing, Ready to sign, With the payer, Denial route\nA request leaves once nothing is left for a person: sent, decided or settled"
  process r2 "**2 Ledger records**\nApproved authorizations with their units and reviews, and requests waiting on a payer\nPlus each request signed and sent in New Case during the demo that the ledger did not have, marked 'New today'"
  process r3 "**3 Dashboard requests in neither list**\nOpen denials, and requests decided or sent since"
  process r4 "**4 Saved New Case drafts** that are not a request yet"
  process r5 "**5 Accepted denials**\nDenial Intelligence closed them"
endgroup

decision d2 "Is the ledger record the same request as a queue row?\n(same ID or case ID)"
process j2 "It joins that row: units used and the review are added, and 'New today' when it applies\nStatus, next action and button stay the request's"
process o2 "A row of its own: Approved, With the payer, Info requested, Denial route, Accepted or Preparing\nWhen its Dashboard request was decided since, the row says so: Approved, Partial approval or Denied"
decision d4 "Does the draft belong to a request already listed?"
process j4 "It stays on that row\nThe row offers 'Open the draft in New Case'"
process o4 "A row of its own in In progress\nIntake not finished, Needs your input, Agents working or Ready to sign"
goto gP "Continues in: Authorizations › In progress › Drafts being prepared"
process j5 "The denial's row reads 'Accepted' in Denied\nNeeds attention, 'Plan the step-down', button 'Open case'"
goto gD "Continues in: Authorizations › Denied › Step-down plans from accepted denials"

group gN "Notes added under the patient"
  process n1 "'New today': a request signed and sent today"
  process n2 "'Updated for a payer change · 10/20': Payers redrafted it"
  process n3 "'Consider a step-down' on R-0873 and P-1522\nHover for 'Day 18 of 21 · aftercare visit not booked yet' or 'Day 11 · IOP starts Monday'"
endgroup
goto gU "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Updated for a payer change"

process st "Only the rows at the sites in view are kept\nA denial follows its own site; everything else follows its case"
goto gSi "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Sites: what each viewer sees"

group gO "Order, before any sort"
  process o1 "By deadline: Act now, then Within 24 hours, then the next 7 days, then later"
  process o3 "Then the rows waiting on a person first"
  process o5 "Then the soonest due, then the lower approval chance, then the ID"
endgroup
process bd "A queue request keeps its own deadline band\nAny other row: overdue or urgent is Act now, under a day is Within 24 hours, under 7 days is the week, else later"
end e1 "One row per request, in that order"
goto gR "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Read a row"

s0 --> r1 --> r2 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| j2
d2 -->|No| o2
j2 --> r3
o2 --> r3
r3 --> r4 --> d4
d4 -->|Yes| j4
d4 -->|No| o4
o4 -.-> gP
j4 --> r5
o4 --> r5
r5 --> j5
j5 -.-> gD
j5 --> n1
r2 -.-> n1
n1 --> n2 --> n3
n2 -.-> gU
n3 --> st
st -.-> gSi
st --> o1 --> o3 --> o5 --> e1
o1 -.-> bd
e1 --> gR
